# Design: One credential option name

## Problem
steelMiddleware and withSteelSession used apiKey while steelScrape exposed steelApiKey for the same Steel credential.

## Approach
v0.3.0 standardizes all three APIs on apiKey before the first npm publication. Runtime exclusivity checks now share the same error and option shape.

## Key trade-offs
- This changes the GitHub-only v0.2.0 source API, but no npm version used the old name.
- A compile-time regression test rejects the legacy spelling so the public surface stays consistent.
